{"title":"2024 SSMO Team Round Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the number of ordered triples of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d80414f2f94f70731e91b6e12c4e6934c8fa65de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> that satisfy the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/967d6e1693589d2707da69000845efa7447d8fe3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(a^b)^c+1=513.\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the sum of the three smallest positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> where the last two digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/3/d434fa4fa611c6f1b63183626d99a36195d33c99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^4$\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/1/ce1ef24f6cf1d8a2ebbbaba89ee70b68c9947414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$01$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> such that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />'s units digit and leading nonzero digit are removed, what remains is a two-digit perfect square. The average of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a right triangle with circumcenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and incenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/6/736f7ac3785ee739f497a1100f321db1481e1cac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/55586794117e77b482295a497a1b55083a9e8171.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AB}{BC} = \\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"72\" height=\"39\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> the projection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the projection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d4d82b157094a623cf465e56ea889ad41edcf85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> be the incenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fd4f5ce77a8f5b40decbd82f44f20d43b1503c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e76cd239b6f2565d2817410edc5cbd49a4508a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> as the incenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/a/0fadb639562a7f9db7952e4ec02e327c5c3118e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OEC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a989650e1850dba32f211ae462a40eca191c9c87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[\\omega_{1}\\omega_{2}I]}{[ABC]}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"63\" height=\"45\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb5756adef5d9a6838491d66d19e87e2feb693c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=AC=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a4826138756e48059393331c30916b2b06430cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=6$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> be the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> be the circle externally tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and tangent to rays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. The distance between the centers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> be the roots of the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5ba394cf5b6ca29ca0cb0081d421beb7fdf77f13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 - 6x^2 - 19x - n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"153\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, what is the least possible positive value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/90431f007b42c425783c23c1afa16420b36d29fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha^3 + \\beta^3 + \\gamma^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2024 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be real numbers that satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/e/88e2c3e9e3311ab437b137ffab00e941f17a3a17.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^3+8ab^2=8b^3+4a^2b=375.\\]\" width=\"232\" height=\"17\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/e/54ebc86e51c6ac465b68ba18bb2485480e360dd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor ab \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"35\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2024 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/1/1f16ad2367a1e18d24bea25121727bde83405bf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le a\\le b\\le c&lt; 229$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"160\" height=\"17\" /> satisfy the congruence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/1/bd10716e9f8f22fc39557320306508c5be3220e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^3 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{229}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"21\" />. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/9/229e6d827039d2f0a926690cdcf8f63026779704.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$71^2 - 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/0/d302d48f0d8509718f6be973a940d0ed469782fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$107^2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" /> are both multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2daa680ee77924479ad0e2f3d30191bcfd2edca7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$229$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2024 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/055dcba798b1424c44c2606d913e0f2edab1c5ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" /> be an equiangular octagon such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc6ff3362601be8ea686a87f08f5ecdce9de7b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=6, BC=8, CD=10, DE=12, EF=6, FG=8, GH=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"516\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/2/cb232bd9cbfbd858fa025916d8fb2b349a0cf15c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />. The radius of the largest circle that fits inside the octagon can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/560d59a8b28eefaa0b822421f1a78e64d155c1c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b\\sqrt{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is a squarefree positive integer. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2024 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The side-lengths of a convex cyclic quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> are integers and satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/b/a1be4c4093d9471e6a47d206bad3aacfe02f3ffb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(AB\\cdot AD+BC\\cdot CD)^2=AC^2\\cdot BD^2-72.\\]\" width=\"339\" height=\"20\" /> Find the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2024 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> denote the set of positive divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/4/9342f5a2cbfd843e9d2cc0d9b81b06258b4226d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5400$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5d4cc0a937f9ae8f1530256fbe1ce6bcfdc1fd9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S_i = \\{d \\mid d \\in S, \\, d \\equiv i \\pmod{4}\\}\\]\" width=\"258\" height=\"18\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/b/d3b63c17213f84d730e0de1f8c08597f7a648e37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> denote the sum of all elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e0ec34cd8860ceb97113f81ba768ba739ad5166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />. Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/3/573a18475c4a2169e8689b1c7de50d4603a4eb70.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s_0^2+s_1^2+s_2^2+s_3^2-2s_0s_2-2s_1s_3.\\]\" width=\"260\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2024 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 11\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the smallest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> with 3 positive prime factors such that for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/1/fd16fdd5d07a5419dc5f7c7259b43f4c5301f950.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^n \\equiv k \\pmod n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2024 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 12\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a deck of 54 cards (2 identical jokers, 4 identical cards with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/7/207a673a15fc91fc08068a0949f18b506af3c95c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,3,\\dots,13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"17\" />), each card is dealt to one of 3 people, each having a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> chance of receiving each card. The expected sum of the number of unique cards the three of them have can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2024 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 13\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/310f72e4a725e4590dcf2dca67597ee57b285288.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"11\" /> be the roots of the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/d/45d666c0c4fa8f4a151c085a38c03c6f3aa2113b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^7+5x^6+9x^5+x^4+x^3+10x^2+5x+1.\\]\" width=\"330\" height=\"17\" /> Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/c/8dc382ad11db01ff3d00a8e17eabe97dc149cefe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left|\\prod_{n=1}^7 \\prod_{m=n+1}^7 (a_na_m-1)\\right|.\\]\" width=\"177\" height=\"54\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2024 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 14\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> inscribed in circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> as the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/a/12a186ad64c2620c417b49a57a2892fb948fa8b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP = 9, CP = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/f/1df7894a0be64bb7434cbe5b49a4ad21c365b8f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" />, find the perimeter of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2024 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 15\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018041606\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.050 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 538/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 17687/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time repor